WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:04.606
The filling unit of line 3 has to keep running for the whole shift.

2
00:00:05.663 --> 00:00:08.565
The module Maintenance goes from breakdown to predictive

3
00:00:08.647 --> 00:00:11.398
and covers the numbers that show whether it works.

4
00:00:12.405 --> 00:00:13.601
You are the engineer.

5
00:00:14.403 --> 00:00:17.456
With the team lead you keep the unit whole through a shift.

6
00:00:18.471 --> 00:00:23.127
First what maintenance you choose and who does it, with strategies and with TPM.

7
00:00:24.204 --> 00:00:26.178
Then how you prepare and measure it,

8
00:00:26.317 --> 00:00:29.568
with planning and spare parts and with measuring maintenance.

9
00:00:30.857 --> 00:00:33.388
The first topic is Maintenance strategies.

10
00:00:34.128 --> 00:00:34.836
There are four.

11
00:00:35.855 --> 00:00:40.743
You repair after the breakdown, at a fixed interval, on condition or on a forecast.

12
00:00:41.802 --> 00:00:44.960
Some parts wear with age and others fail at random.

13
00:00:45.664 --> 00:00:48.021
A fixed interval does not fit everything.

14
00:00:49.054 --> 00:00:52.374
You read the failure rate against age in a bathtub curve,

15
00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:54.824
though it holds for only some equipment.

16
00:00:56.182 --> 00:00:59.653
The second topic is TPM and autonomous maintenance.

17
00:01:00.373 --> 00:01:02.823
Operators do the basic care themselves.

18
00:01:03.878 --> 00:01:06.804
They clean, inspect, lubricate and tighten.

19
00:01:07.539 --> 00:01:09.478
Anything that is off gets a tag.

20
00:01:10.479 --> 00:01:13.834
The checks are on a CILT standard at the unit.

21
00:01:15.211 --> 00:01:18.392
The third topic is Planning, scheduling and spare parts.

22
00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:24.253
You prepare a job with steps, parts and tools before anyone picks up a spanner.

23
00:01:25.353 --> 00:01:28.848
Then you fill the week with jobs, up to the hours available.

24
00:01:29.839 --> 00:01:33.822
On the laptop is the CMMS, from notification to closing.

25
00:01:35.138 --> 00:01:37.518
The fourth topic is Measuring maintenance.

26
00:01:38.219 --> 00:01:41.655
You count how often the unit stops and how long it takes.

27
00:01:42.662 --> 00:01:46.354
You also look at how many of all the hours were planned work.

28
00:01:47.393 --> 00:01:51.085
Where a technician’s time goes, you measure with work sampling.

29
00:01:52.113 --> 00:01:56.269
That is how the filling unit of line 3 stays whole for the whole shift.

30
00:01:57.594 --> 00:01:58.395
The whole map.

31
00:01:59.123 --> 00:02:02.617
The third station is Maintenance, in Keeping the plant running.

32
00:02:03.617 --> 00:02:05.811
Each of the four topics has four levels.

33
00:02:06.832 --> 00:02:10.327
Start at Basics level with the four maintenance strategies.

34
00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:13.057
They tell you what fits each machine.

35
00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:17.375
At Working knowledge level come failure, writing a standard,

36
00:02:17.549 --> 00:02:19.859
planning the work and where the hours go.

37
00:02:20.875 --> 00:02:24.497
At Advanced level come condition monitoring, the seven steps,

38
00:02:24.659 --> 00:02:27.051
spare parts and a set of KPIs.

39
00:02:28.222 --> 00:02:31.937
At Expert level come reviewing a plan, TPM as a programme,

40
00:02:32.088 --> 00:02:33.957
planned shutdowns and the cost.

41
00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:39.082
Every lesson and every film in this module has a place on this map.
